\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Positioning of the present contribution against the closest prior systems. Existing quantization work optimizes per-layer precision without exploiting linguistic structure of the target language; the present work is orthogonal, adding a typology-aware cache layer that can be composed with any of these compression backbones. $\checkmark  $ = explicit support, $\times $ = no support, \emph  {implicit} = present but not analyzed. ``---'' marks headline numbers that the cited paper's abstract or public table does not state in a verbatim form; the qualitative column entry stands in those cases.}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:positioning}{{1}{4}{Positioning of the present contribution against the closest prior systems. Existing quantization work optimizes per-layer precision without exploiting linguistic structure of the target language; the present work is orthogonal, adding a typology-aware cache layer that can be composed with any of these compression backbones. $\checkmark $ = explicit support, $\times $ = no support, \emph {implicit} = present but not analyzed. ``---'' marks headline numbers that the cited paper's abstract or public table does not state in a verbatim form; the qualitative column entry stands in those cases}{table.1}{}}
