\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Composition of the 272-d tonal-perceptual fingerprint: tone histogram (6) $+$ temporal-subsampled MFCC ($130$) $+$ MFCC first-difference ($130$) $+$ F0 statistics (4) $+$ energy statistics (2). Segment widths are proportional to dimension count. The 6-d tone histogram is Vietnamese-orthography-tuned; the segmental components (MFCC + $\Delta $ + F0 + energy) carry phrase-level identity. The two-stream voting architecture (\S  \ref {sec:method:twostream}) treats component A as an independent 6-d tone stream $f_A$ and components B+C+D+E as a 260-d segmental stream $f_B$ rather than a single concatenated vector.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fp_composition}{{2}{6}{Composition of the 272-d tonal-perceptual fingerprint: tone histogram (6) $+$ temporal-subsampled MFCC ($130$) $+$ MFCC first-difference ($130$) $+$ F0 statistics (4) $+$ energy statistics (2). Segment widths are proportional to dimension count. The 6-d tone histogram is Vietnamese-orthography-tuned; the segmental components (MFCC + $\Delta $ + F0 + energy) carry phrase-level identity. The two-stream voting architecture (\S \ref {sec:method:twostream}) treats component A as an independent 6-d tone stream $f_A$ and components B+C+D+E as a 260-d segmental stream $f_B$ rather than a single concatenated vector}{figure.2}{}}
